    {
      "version": "0.4.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "fundamentals_screen.core_sub_screens.earnings_growth: added explicit scoring_curve — the book gives a floor (20%) and a 'reward above' threshold (30%) but never specifies how a value between/beyond those becomes a 0-1 score. Selected: linear from 0 at the 20% floor to 1.0 at 60% (2x the reward threshold), capped at 1.0 beyond. Verified against the worked EGX example: 59.8% growth scores 0.995.",
        "fundamentals_screen.modifiers.deceleration_flag: added explicit penalty_formula — same category of gap as earnings_growth, now resolved. Penalty scales linearly from 0 (current growth >= trailing average) to the full -0.15 cap at a >=50% relative drop from the trailing average. Trailing average window set to the book's own recommendation (ch07-notes.md: 4-8 quarter rolling average, defaulting to 4). Verified against the book's own worked example (80%->65%->28%): produces the full -0.15 penalty, consistent with the book calling this 'a real warning sign.'"
      ],
      "source": "chat decision — explicit default selected and verified, not left ambiguous for Claude Code to guess"
    },
