    {
      "version": "0.8.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "fundamentals_screen.modifiers.peg_modifier: RESOLVED exact formula. Claude Code proposed a linear formula (clamp(-0.10*(peg-1), -0.10, 0.10)); rejected after verification showed it was only symmetric algebraically, not in practice — it caps at PEG=0 (unreachable for a real profitable stock) on the low side vs PEG=2 (realistic) on the high side, meaning the full +0.10 boost could almost never actually trigger. Replaced with a log-distance formula (clamp(-0.10*log2(peg), -0.10, 0.10)), which caps symmetrically and realistically at PEG=0.5/PEG=2, and makes the book's own worked PEG example (0.5) land exactly on the +0.10 cap instead of an arbitrary half-value"
      ],
      "source": "Claude Code build question — proposed formula checked numerically before accepting, not approved on read"
    },
    {
      "version": "0.9.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "category_tagging.category_overrides.turnaround: RESOLVED the full earnings_growth curve override, not just the floor. Claude Code correctly caught that a floor-only override (100%) was mathematically broken against the unchanged normal cap (60%). Rejected a proposed uniform 5x scale (floor=100%, cap=300%): valid math, but requires an unreachable 300% growth outlier to max out, and contradicts ch06-notes.md's explicit statement that magnitude above the floor is NOT the real signal for turnarounds. Resolved instead by preserving the normal curve's absolute 40-percentage-point ramp width, relocated to the new floor (floor=100%, cap=140%) — a real, confirmed turnaround now reaches full marks around 140-150% instead of needing 300%"
      ],
      "source": "Claude Code build question — proposed formula checked numerically and against book text before accepting"
    },
    {
      "version": "0.10.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "fundamentals_screen.core_sub_screens.earnings_acceleration/code_33: RESOLVED how 'unconfirmed' (cross-source-flip) sub-screens affect the composite — same exclude+renormalize mechanism as partial_data_handling, distinguished by reason tag ('unconfirmed' vs 'missing_data') for logging",
        "fundamentals_screen.scoring_architecture: added exclusion_weight_safeguard, NOT part of Claude Code's original proposal. Stress-tested the recommended mechanism against a realistic compounding case (one source-switch event knocking out both earnings_acceleration and code_33 at once, 0.40 of total weight) and found it would silently inflate earnings_growth's effective weight by 1.67x — the opposite of cautious, given ch07-notes.md calls acceleration the single most important fundamental signal. Added a 0.35 total-excluded-weight threshold above which the result is flagged low_confidence_fundamentals_screen for ai_synthesis to discount, rather than being silently renormalized and ranked normally"
      ],
      "source": "Claude Code build question — core mechanism accepted, but stress-tested against compounding with Section 2.4's existing exclusion before signing off"
