    {
      "version": "0.15.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "market_regime_gate.new_high_low_ratio_favorable: RESOLVED the vague 'trending up' into an exact two-point comparison (ratio[t] > ratio[t-21]), matching tt_4's own precedent instead of leaving a second vague trend-check in the same config that already fixed this once",
        "market_regime_gate.new_high_low_ratio_favorable: fixed a real division-by-zero risk -- count(52wk_low) can legitimately be 0 on a strong day, which would make the raw ratio undefined/infinite. Denominator changed to count(52wk_low)+1, a standard minimal-distortion fix, not a change to the book's own ratio concept",
        "market_regime_gate is now fully specified with no remaining ambiguous language or unhandled edge cases -- ready for a rules doc / build handoff"
