    {
      "version": "0.16.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "market_regime_gate.leader_pullback_shallow.metric: CORRECTED '21-day' to '20-day' local high window -- a real discrepancy against feature-03-market-regime-gate-rules.md Section 2.3's explicit instruction to reuse leader_divergence's window rather than invent a third. Caught by Claude Code during implementation, confirmed correct by this reviewer, fixed in code and spec together.",
        "market_regime_gate.leader_pullback_shallow.days_since_local_high_tie_handling: NEW. Real bug found via independent testing that the delivered fixture suite didn't happen to cover -- a price plateau at the local high causes naive argmax() to count from the FIRST day of the plateau, not the most recent, overstating pullback duration. Directly relevant to this project given NDRL is already documented as a thin/flat-trading EGX ticker. Fix: reverse the window before argmax so ties resolve to the most recent occurrence."
      ],
      "source": "independent testing beyond the delivered fixture suite -- found via a plateau-price test case Claude Code's own fixtures didn't happen to include"
    },
    {
      "version": "0.17.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "risk_rules.defensive_mode.trigger/revert_when: RESOLVED from vague ('meaningfully below baseline') to an exact formula (rolling_win_loss_ratio < 2.0 OR rolling_win_rate < 0.50, trailing 20 trades). Original win-rate-only framing was flagged as contradicting a principle already stated elsewhere in this file (graduation_criteria's own note that win_rate alone isn't sufficient) -- not just imprecise, actually inconsistent with itself.",
        "risk_rules.defensive_mode.relationship_to_performance_scaling: NEW. Reconciled two previously-unaddressed, potentially-conflicting mechanisms (position_sizing's stepped losing-streak reduction vs risk_rules' flat defensive_mode multiplier) -- confirmed both are real, distinct book concepts, and specified multiplicative stacking when both are active simultaneously, justified by the project's own stated risk-first philosophy since the book doesn't address this compounding case directly.",
        "risk_rules.stop_loss.target_avg_realized_loss_pct_note: NEW. Reclassified this figure as a monitoring statistic, not an enforceable rule -- it was sitting alongside hard_max_pct as if it were the same kind of thing, but you cannot code 'average realized losses to 6.5%' the way you can code a hard ceiling.",
        "risk_rules.profit_protection.initial_stop_distance_definition: NEW. Surfaced a real gap -- only the 10% ceiling was ever defined, never how a given trade's actual stop distance is set under that ceiling. Given an honest v1 interim default (flat 10%) with the proper technical-level resolution explicitly deferred to entry_timing, which doesn't exist yet -- a real cross-feature dependency, not silently glossed over.",
        "risk_rules.exit_signals_beyond_stop.largest_decline_since_entry: 'above-average volume' now defined as the 50-day average, reusing entry_timing's already-established volume convention instead of inventing a fourth number.",
        "risk_rules.exit_signals_beyond_stop.post_earnings_reaction_failure: now explicitly calls for reusing fundamentals_screen.score_price_reaction_to_earnings() rather than reimplementing the same logic separately -- same canonical-implementation standard already enforced twice elsewhere in this project."
      ],
      "source": "chat review of risk_rules and position_sizing against ch12-notes.md, ch13-notes.md, and manifesto.md Parts 7-9 -- first review of these blocks since the project's original seed files"
