    {
      "version": "0.19.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "entry_timing.vcp_detection: REPLACED vague 'swing high/low detection, then measure sequential contraction depths' with a fully-specified architecture. Parameters locked from two rounds of visual calibration on real EGX tickers (COMI, TMGH, SWDY, TRTO): ATR_MULTIPLIER=1.0 (1.5x rejected -- missed real COMI structure), SMOOTHING_WINDOW=5 rolling median (not mean -- median ignores single-day thin-trading spikes), DISTANCE_DAYS=3 (5 was too coarse for tight handle contractions), DISTANCE_WEEKS=2 (stable across both passes).",
        "entry_timing.vcp_detection: Added dual-timeframe architecture (weekly-first to validate macro base, daily to resolve internal contractions) -- confirmed necessary from TMGH calibration chart where daily showed a nonsensical 8-contraction base that the weekly correctly reduced to one clean base.",
        "entry_timing.vcp_detection: Added tick-quantized pre-filter (minimum 20 unique closing prices) -- TRTO confirmed this class of EGX penny stock produces zero meaningful peaks regardless of parameters, should be filtered before detection runs.",
        "entry_timing.vcp_detection: Added 325-day hard maximum base duration cutoff applied BEFORE monotonicity filter -- TMGH chart confirmed order matters.",
        "entry_timing.vcp_detection: RESOLVED contraction_sequence_monotonicity_filter from 'roughly halving' (uncodeable) to an exact two-rule formula. ONE ITEM STILL OPEN: the tolerance for rule_b (110% vs 130%) needs an explicit decision before Feature 5 test file is written -- SWDY's real base is the boundary case, documented with worked checks in the new block."
      ],
