    {
      "version": "0.27.0-draft",
      "changes": [
        "PHILOSOPHY CHANGE: profit-first principle applied within book rules — where the book gives a range or option, always take the more aggressive choice that maximizes gain potential",
        "market_regime_gate.gate_logic: AND → OR. Book describes three signals to watch, not three simultaneous requirements. Any one confirming signal opens the gate.",
        "fundamentals_screen: REBUILT from scratch. Replaced weighted composite (6 sub-screens, invented weights, 65-point threshold, required 5+ quarters, max score 35) with 3 yes/no questions directly from ch07-notes.md. Question 1: EPS growth ≥20% (required). Question 2: acceleration from prior quarter (skipped if only 1 quarter available). Question 3: revenue growing (skipped if unavailable). Simple, works with limited data, book-faithful.",
        "position_sizing: default positions changed from 4 to 6 — top of book's stated 4-6 range for small accounts",
        "position_sizing: sizing changed from 25% (4 positions) to 16.7% (6 positions) — same capital, more concurrent opportunities",
        "position_sizing.losing_streak_response: REMOVED specific step-down triggers (3 stops → 40%, 5 stops → 20%). These were invented numbers. Book says reduce during losing streaks without giving specific triggers. Defensive mode handles sustained underperformance instead.",
        "risk_rules.defensive_mode.trigger: loosened from (ratio < 2.0 OR rate < 0.50) to (ratio < 1.5 OR rate < 0.40) — less aggressive trigger, more time at full size",
        "position_sizing.reentry_from_cash: pilot size increased from 50% to 75% — faster capital deployment while still starting smaller than full size",
        "entry_timing.pivot_point.buy_trigger: breakout volume threshold lowered from 1.4x to 1.2x — 1.4x was invented, book says meaningfully above average"
      ],
